## Approval

Applying these changes requires all of:

```bash
make upgrade-pve1 EXTRA_JSON='{"allow_repo_change_pve1":true,"repo_change_confirmation_pve1":"{{ repo_change_confirmation_pve1_required }}","allow_upgrade_pve1":true,"upgrade_confirmation_pve1":"{{ upgrade_confirmation_pve1_required }}","console_access_confirmed_pve1":true}'
```

`console_access_confirmed_pve1` is your assertion that you have physical, IPMI
or KVM access to {{ expected_hostname }}. Do not upgrade without it: if the
network configuration does not survive the reboot, SSH will not save you.

## Rollback

There is no supported downgrade from PVE 9 to PVE 8. Rollback for this host means
**restore from the verified archives** (see docs/rollback.md), which is why stage
6b refuses to run until stage 4b has passed.
